WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:08.727
- I am so sorry I missed
you the first time.

00:00:08.727 --> 00:00:10.980
- That's okay.
- I was sick.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.360
Your co-star though, hosted.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.459
- Yeah, Kumail, he did a good job.

00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:15.660
- Didn't do as good as
this is going to be.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.493
I'm just kidding,

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:17.326
I'm just kidding.
(Quentin laughing)

00:00:17.326 --> 00:00:18.159
I'm just kidding.

00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:19.387
Anyway, let's talk about the new show

00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:20.850
"Tiny Beautiful Things."
- Yes, yes.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.650
- That's an intense scene we just saw,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.834
so who do you play?

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:27.480
- I am Danny, I play
the husband to Claire,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.190
played beautifully by Kathryn Hahn.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.023
- Mm, love her.

00:00:30.023 --> 00:00:33.990
- And we're just kind of going
through the everyday life,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.640
you know, being married,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.040
having a 16 year old
daughter, trying to raise her

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.720
while she's going through her transitions

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.300
and us having our problems ourselves

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.820
and trying to find ourselves really.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.710
- Yeah.
- And it's--

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.180
- Which can be difficult if you do this.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.090
- Exactly, growing apart,
it's grounded and it's messy

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.610
and I'm just really
excited to be a part of it.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.443
Beautiful show.

00:00:54.443 --> 00:00:55.920
- Did you know her before this?

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.390
- I did not, I did not.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.700
- So wait, you're in such
an intense relationship

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.783
in this movie,

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.980
so how did y'all kind of
start that relationship off.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.270
Did y'all do anything to prepare?

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.150
- I mean the casting
process was really fast too.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.230
Got casted on a Sunday

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.750
and we had to be going 10 days after that.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.583
- Wow.

00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:18.240
- Yeah, we wanted to bring to
life this 16 year relationship

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.770
between the two of us, at the very least,

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.690
'cause that's the age of our daughter.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:22.710
And so we decided to meet,

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.610
we decided to go on a hike

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.820
and we did this thing
to have the 36 questions

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.064
to fall in love with somebody.

00:01:28.064 --> 00:01:28.920
- Wait, what?

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.753
Is that a thing?

00:01:29.753 --> 00:01:30.586
- Yeah.

00:01:30.586 --> 00:01:31.419
- How have I never heard of this.

00:01:31.419 --> 00:01:32.610
- Like a New York Times article.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.100
So we go through and we're hiking

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.360
and we're asking each
other these questions

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.860
and Kathryn comes up with the idea like,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.830
we shouldn't just answer as ourselves,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.360
we should answer as our character.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.410
- Oh, smart.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.710
- So then we're doing
this and we kind of find

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.197
our backstory together in these questions.

00:01:49.197 --> 00:01:50.580
- And then develop that chemistry.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.080
- Yeah and it was just super organic.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.060
- What are the questions like?

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.040
- Well actually, I brought a
few of them, if you want...

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.960
- I want to know them.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.972
- Obviously I need help falling
in love. (audience laughs)

00:02:00.972 --> 00:02:02.373
Like whatever.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.313
- Okay, all right cool.

00:02:04.313 --> 00:02:05.960
So let me see, a good one for you.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.660
So they have ones like this, it's like,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.130
would you like to be famous?

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:11.963
In what way?

00:02:11.963 --> 00:02:13.110
And that's not a great question for you,

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.880
'cause you're famous. (audience laughing)

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.080
So we're not going to do that.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.150
- Let's set that one on fire. (laughing)

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.290
That ship has sailed.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.550
- Okay this is a good one.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.620
Before making a telephone call,

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.680
do you ever rehearse what
you're going to say? And why?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.573
- Okay, no, but I should. (laughing)

00:02:32.712 --> 00:02:35.190
I should definitely at least
have some bullet points.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.023
- And see that's my thing,

00:02:36.023 --> 00:02:37.800
I like to rehearse and
then I like to make sure

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.060
I say it in the best way.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.560
Because sometimes--
- That's smart.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.060
You're going to do well in relationships.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.855
- It just comes off.

00:02:43.855 --> 00:02:45.150
We'll see.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.650
Is there one more, lets do one more.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.483
- Yeah, yeah, let's do this.

00:02:47.483 --> 00:02:48.630
And this one I love.
- I want to do one more.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:49.650
I love this by the way.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.640
What a cool way to connect.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.960
You should do this with every person

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:52.793
you do a movie with.

00:02:52.793 --> 00:02:54.466
- I don't want everyone to
fall in love with me though.

00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:55.860
(audience laughing)
- Yeah you do.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:56.730
Yeah you do.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.080
Then you shouldn't have walked out here

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.133
looking like that.

00:03:00.006 --> 00:03:01.920
- Put the button back.
- That's your problem.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:02.753
- Yeah exactly.

00:03:02.753 --> 00:03:03.960
Okay for this one.
- Okay, one more.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.693
- So for what in your life
do you feel most grateful?

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.260
- Oh this is going to be a cheesy answer,

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.390
but it's my children and here's why.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.950
Because I didn't think
I'd ever get married

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:14.940
or have children.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.160
Not because I'm frowning
upon either one of them,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.440
just because I've always been a very...

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.310
I'm a musician at heart,

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.530
I'm kind of just always this wonder

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:23.850
and I love wondering

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.370
and so I never thought
that would happen to me.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.110
So that's pretty magical

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.730
to have loved someone deeply

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.950
and to have children is pretty great.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.190
- 100%, that's so interesting,
not to go off on...

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.180
When I watched you on "The Voice"

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.780
you have such a motherly loving vibe.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.640
- Which is so weird,

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.947
no one that knew me before
would ever have been like,

00:03:44.947 --> 00:03:46.200
"you're going to be a mom." (laughing)

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.610
- Wow.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:51.030
- Just because I'm naturally that person

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.330
that I feel like a lot
of artists in general

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.280
unfortunately can get a bit selfish

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.850
because you're so consumed
with whatever you're doing

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.223
and is always a high
priority in your life.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.290
I feel like I lived my 20s
pretty selfishly in a good way.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.370
Like I got to travel the world,

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.418
got to do all these things.

00:04:09.418 --> 00:04:12.180
Where I'm from, you're like
dead if you have babies at 31.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.550
So you're like an old maid.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.860
So I started late in the
game from where I'm from,

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.090
but I love that I waited

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.950
because now I really appreciated that time

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.320
and now I get to appreciate
these little beings

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.153
that are so magical.

00:04:23.153 --> 00:04:24.090
- That's awesome.
- Yeah.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.641
Can sometimes be hard. (laughing)

00:04:25.641 --> 00:04:26.724
(audience clapping)

00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:27.750
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.583
For sure.

00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:30.210
- They give you gray hair, but it's fine.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.130
Okay, let's do another commercial break.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.420
Everybody I love those questions.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.880
You can see "Tiny
Beautiful Things" on Hulu.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.143
It's streaming now.

